###### h4

THE WALLRAF IS CLOSED\.\.\.

###### p

After 25 successful years with more than 4 million visitors, the Wallraf\-Richartz Museum is in urgent need of renovation\. To ensure that the iconic building designed by star architect Oswald Mathias Ungers continues to shine as a beacon of Cologne culture in the future, the museum is closed for a two\-year general renovation until the end of 2028\.&nbsp;
###### p

During this time, the entire museum will be closed\. Our artworks will not be shown at other locations either\. But you can already look forward to a new Wallraf\. Late&nbsp;2028, the ‘old’ renovated Ungers building and the ‘new’ extension by Swiss architects Christ & Gantenbein will reopen as one large, combined Wallraf\-Richartz Museum & Fondation Corboud\. Rest assured: it will be worth the wait\!
